WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.837
Every control in the book follows the
same path, and every step has a way back.

2
00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.376
Start with an inventory.

3
00:00:06.376 --> 00:00:11.087
Purview's content explorer exports
where sensitive information types and

4
00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:15.725
labels already sit, one type at a time,
so the rollout starts where the risk is.

5
00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:17.606
Treat it as a dated snapshot:

6
00:00:17.606 --> 00:00:22.350
counts can take up to seven days to
update, and fourteen for SharePoint.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.835
Then a signed decision record,
and the build, as code,

8
00:00:25.835 --> 00:00:30.813
in a test tenant first, because some
label changes can't be cleanly undone.

9
00:00:30.813 --> 00:00:32.024
Then a pilot ring.

10
00:00:32.024 --> 00:00:35.100
For D L P, simulation is the pilot.

11
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.575
It runs for up to fifteen days and keeps
its data for thirty, so export the matches.

12
00:00:40.575 --> 00:00:45.404
It evaluates existing SharePoint and
OneDrive content, but only new mail,

13
00:00:45.404 --> 00:00:49.837
Teams and device activity, so let
those run through a business cycle.

14
00:00:49.837 --> 00:00:53.812
Then enforce ring by ring, and
validate with a labeled sample.

15
00:00:53.812 --> 00:00:57.912
And rollback never means deleting
a label, because content keeps it.

16
00:00:57.912 --> 00:00:59.640
You unpublish it instead.
